Creating Release Tarballs
==========================

Use the make targets to create release tarballs (similar to kernel's perf-tar-src-pkg):

  make tarxz-pkg     - Create .tar.xz release tarball (recommended)
  make targz-pkg     - Create .tar.gz release tarball
  make tarbz2-pkg    - Create .tar.bz2 release tarball
  make tar-pkg       - Create .tar release tarball

Tarballs are created in the current working directory by default.
Set TARBALL_DIR environment variable to override:

  TARBALL_DIR=~/rpmbuild/SOURCES make tarxz-pkg

Each tarball includes:
  - All files listed in MANIFEST
  - A HEAD file containing the git SHA (for build container tracking)
  - Version-prefixed directory structure: dwarves-X.Y/

Version is automatically calculated as: (latest_tag_minor + 1)
Example: if latest tag is v1.31, tarball will be dwarves-1.32.tar.xz

Implementation: scripts/make-tarball.sh
